MIDI tap, USB side: every USB-MIDI event packet that comes in is copied to fm1-base's MIDI tap (device/midi_tap.c,
patches/fm1-base/0001-midi-tap.patch) before usb.c sorts it, so a monitor sees SysEx, system common, active sensing
and reset too, which plat_midi_in leaves out. Only when FM1B_MIDI_TAP is defined (fm1-base's unity.c, with the tap).
Why MIDIMON needs it: it is a MIDI monitor; plat_midi_in drops what it must show.
Applies to: felucca-bsp d6b8f77 (fm1-base aa2b3bc). Upstream: not offered yet.
diff --git a/chip/usb.c b/chip/usb.c
index bdf6769..5834c79 100644
